<title>UK: British election diary - April 24.</title>
<headline>British election diary - April 24.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a list of events in the British election campaign on Friday -</p>
<p>0730 GMT - Labour leader Tony Blair holds a news conference with the party's home affairs spokesman Jack Straw and economics spokesman Gordon Brown. Blair then leaves for campaign visits to south-east England.</p>
<p>0815 GMT - Prime Minister John Major hosts a news conference at Conservative headquarters. Major then leaves for a campaign trip in south-east England. -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
